{
  "title": "70: Al-Ma'arij المعارج",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسَاَلَ سَآئِلٌ ۢ بِعَذَابٍ وَّاقِعٍۙ‏(1)\nSA-ALA SAAA-ELUM BE-A’ZAABINW WAAQE’.\nAn asker asked for a punishment sure to befall\nلِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ لَيْسَ لَهٗ دَافِعٌ ۙ‏(2)\nLIL-KAAFEREENA LAYSA LAHU DAAFE’.\n—which none can avert from the faithless —\nمِّنَ اللّٰهِ ذِى الْمَعَارِجِؕ‏(3)\nMENAL LAAHE ZIL MA-A’AREJ.\nfrom Allah, Lord of the lofty stations.\nتَعْرُجُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ وَ الرُّوْحُ اِلَيْهِ فِىْ يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهٗ خَمْسِيْنَ اَلْفَ سَنَةٍ‌ۚ‏(4)\nTA’ROJUL MALAAA-EKATO WAR ROOHO ELAYHE FEE YAWMIN KAANA MIQDAAROHU KHAMSEENA ALFA SANAH.\nThe angels and the Spirit ascend to Him in a day whose span is fifty thousand years.\nفَاصْبِرْ صَبْرًا جَمِيْلًا‏(5)\nFASBIR SABRAN JAMEELAA.\nSo be patient, with a patience that is graceful.\nاِنَّهُمْ يَرَوْنَهٗ بَعِيْدًا ۙ‏(6)\nINNAHUM YARAWNAHU BA-E’EDAA.\nIndeed they see it to be far off,\nوَّنَرٰٮهُ قَرِيْبًا ؕ‏(7)\nWA NARAAHO QAREEBAA.\nand We see it to be near.\nيَوْمَ تَكُوْنُ السَّمَآءُ كَالْمُهْلِۙ‏(8)\nYAWMA TAKOONUS SAMAAA-O KAL-MOHL.\nThe day when the sky will be like molten copper,\nوَتَكُوْنُ الْجِبَالُ كَالْعِهْنِۙ‏(9)\nWA TAKOONUL JEBAALO KAL-E’HN.\nand the mountains like [tufts of] dyed wool,\nوَلَا يَسْئَلُ حَمِيْمٌ حَمِيْمًا ۖۚ‏(10)\nWA LAA YAS-ALO HAMEEMUN HAMEEMAA.\nand no friend will inquire about [the welfare of his] friend,\nيُّبَصَّرُوْنَهُمْ‌ؕ يَوَدُّ الْمُجْرِمُ لَوْ يَفْتَدِىْ مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمِئِذٍۢ بِبَنِيْهِۙ‏(11)\nYOBASSAROONAHUM, YAWADDUL MUJREMO LAW YAFTADEE MIN A’ZAABE YAWME-EZIM BE-BANEEH.\n[though] they will be placed within each other’s sight. The guilty one will wish he could ransom himself from the punishment of that day at the price of his children,\nوَ صَاحِبَتِهٖ وَاَخِيْهِۙ‏(12)\nWA SAAHEBATEHI WA AKHEEH.\nhis spouse and his brother,\nوَفَصِيْلَتِهِ الَّتِىْ تُئْوِيْهِۙ‏(13)\nWA FASEELATEHIL LATEE TOAWEEH.\nhis kin, which had sheltered him\nوَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ۙ ثُمَّ يُنْجِيْهِۙ‏(14)\nWA MAN FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’N, SUMMA YUNJEEH.\nand all those who are upon the earth, if that might deliver him.\nكَلَّاؕ اِنَّهَا لَظٰىۙ‏(15)\nKALLAA, INNAHAA LAZAA.\nNever! Indeed, it is a blazing fire,\nنَزَّاعَةً لِّلشَّوٰى‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(16)\nNAZZAA-A’TAL LISH-SHAWAA.\nwhich strips away the scalp.\nتَدْعُوْا مَنْ اَدْبَرَ وَتَوَلّٰىۙ‏(17)\nTAD-O’O MAN ADBARA WA TAWALLAA.\nIt invites him, who has turned back [from the truth] and forsaken [it],\nوَجَمَعَ فَاَوْعٰى‏(18)\nWA JAMA-A’ FA-AW-A’A.\namassing [wealth] and hoarding [it].\nاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ خُلِقَ هَلُوْعًا ۙ‏(19)\nINNAL INSAANA KHOLEQA HALOO-A’A.\nIndeed man has been created covetous:\nاِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ جَزُوْعًا ۙ‏(20)\nEZAA MASSAHUSH SHARRO JAZOO-A’A.\nanxious when an ill befalls him\nوَاِذَا مَسَّهُ الْخَيْرُ مَنُوْعًا ۙ‏(21)\nWA EZAA MASSAHUL KHAYRO MANOO-A’A.\nand grudging [charity] when good comes his way\nاِلَّا الْمُصَلِّيْنَۙ‏(22)\nILLAL MOSALLEEN.\n—[all are such] except the prayerful,\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَاتِهِمْ دَآئِمُوْنَۙ‏(23)\nLAZEENA HUM A’LAA SALAATEHIM DAAA-EMOON.\nthose who persevere in their prayers\nوَالَّذِيْنَ فِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(24)\nWAL LAZEENA FEE AMWAALEHIM HAQQUM MA’LOOM.\nand there is a known share in whose wealth\nلِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِۙ‏(25)\nLIS-SAAA-ELE WAL MAHROOM.\nfor the beggar and the deprived,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُصَدِّقُوْنَ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(26)\nWAL LAZEENA YOSADDEQOONA BE-YAWMID DEEN.\nand who affirm the Day of Retribution,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّشْفِقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(27)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM MIN A’ZAABE RABBEHIM MUSHFEQOON.\nand those who are apprehensive of the punishment of their Lord\nاِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّهِمْ غَيْرُ مَاْمُوْنٍ‏(28)\nINNA A’ZAABA RABBEHIM GHAYRO MAAMOON.\n(there is indeed no security from the punishment of their Lord)\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِفُرُوْجِهِمْ حٰفِظُوْنَۙ‏(29)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LE-FOROOJEHIM HAAFEZOON.\nand those who guard their private parts\nاِلَّا عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِهِمْ اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُوْمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(30)\nILLAA A’LAA AZWAAJEHIM AW MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOHUM FA-INNAHUM GHAYRO MALOOMEEN.\n(apart from their spouses and their slave women, for then they are not blameworthy;\nفَمَنِ ابْتَغٰى وَرَآءَ ذٰلِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْعٰدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(31)\nFAMANIB TAGHAA WARAAA-A ZAALEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL A’ADOON.\nbut whoever seeks beyond that—it is they who are the transgressors)\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِاَمٰنٰتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رٰعُوْنَ ۙ‏(32)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LE-AMAANAATEHIM WA A’HDEHIM RAA-O’ON.\nand those who keep their trusts and covenants,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِشَهٰدٰتِهِمْ قَآئِمُوْنَ ۙ‏(33)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-SHAHAADAATEHIM QAAA-EMOON.\nand those who are observant of their testimonies,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَؕ‏(34)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’LAA SALAATEHIM YOHAAFEZOON.\nand those who are watchful of their prayers.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ مُّكْرَمُوْنَؕ‏(35)\nOOLAAA-EKA FEE JANNAATIM MUKRAMOON.\nThey will be in gardens, held in honour.\nفَمَالِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا قِبَلَكَ مُهْطِعِيْنَۙ‏(36)\nFAMAALIL LAZEENA KAFAROO QEBALAKA MOHTE-E’EN.\nWhat is the matter with the faithless that they scramble toward you,\nعَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَعَنِ الشِّمَالِ عِزِيْنَ‏(37)\nA’NIL YAMEENE WA A’NISH SHEMAALE E’ZEEN.\nfrom left and right, in groups?\nاَيَطْمَعُ كُلُّ امْرِىءٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّدْخَلَ جَنَّةَ نَعِيْمٍۙ‏(38)\nAYATMA-O’ KULLUM RE-IM MINHUM AN-Y YUDKHALA JANNATA NA-E’EM.\nDoes each man among them hope to enter the garden of bliss?\nكَلَّا ؕ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُمْ مِّمَّا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(39)\nKALLAA, INNAA KHALAQNAAHUM MIMMAA YA’LAMOON.\nNever! Indeed, We created them from what they know.\nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِرَبِّ الْمَشٰرِقِ وَالْمَغٰرِبِ اِنَّا لَقٰدِرُوْنَۙ‏(40)\nFALAA UQSEMO BE-RABBIL MASHAAREQE WAL MAGHAAREBE INNAA LA-QAADEROON.\nSo I swear by the Lord of the easts and the wests that We are able\nعَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّبَدِّلَ خَيْرًا مِّنْهُمْۙ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَسْبُوْقِيْنَ‏(41)\nA’LAA AN NOBADDELA KHAYRAM MINHUM, WA MAA NAHNO BE-MASBOOQEEN.\nto replace them with [others] better than them and We are not to be outmaneuvered.\nفَذَرْهُمْ يَخُوْضُوْا وَيَلْعَبُوْا حَتّٰى يُلٰقُوْا يَوْمَهُمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(42)\nFA-ZARHUM YAKHOOZOO WA YAL-A’BOO HATTAA YOLAAQOO YAWMAHOMUL LAZEE YOO-A’DOON.\nSo leave them to gossip and play till they encounter the day they are promised:\nيَوْمَ يَخْرُجُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَجْدَاثِ سِرَاعًا كَاَنَّهُمْ اِلٰى نُصُبٍ يُّوْفِضُوْنَۙ‏(43)\nYAWMA YAKHROJOONA MENAL AJDAASE SERAA-A’N KA-ANNAHUM ELAA NOSOBIN-Y YOOFEZOON.\nthe day when they emerge from graves, hastening, as if racing toward a target,\nخَاشِعَةً اَبْصَارُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ ؕ ذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمُ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(44)\nKHAASHE-A’TAN ABSAAROHUM TARHAQOHUM ZILLAH, ZAALEKAL YAWMUL LAZEE KAANOO YOO-A’DOON.\nwith a humbled look [in their eyes], overcast by abasement. That is the day they had been promised.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Ma-a’arij (The Ways of Ascent)\nThis Surah has 44 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is equivalent to the total number of people who keep up prayer and safeguard the property which has been entrusted to them.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will have his sins hidden on the Day of Judgement and he will enter Jannah alongside the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). If a prisoner recites this Surah, he will secure his release. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that if this Surah is recited before sleeping, one keeps safe from the temptations of Shaitan."
}
